From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:21:44 -0500
Subject: ui: the passkey dialogs name Stedding

The list of places to save a passkey said "Your Chrome profile", which a
user meets as soon as Touch ID passkeys work, and the Bluetooth question said
Chrome needs permission. Both are literal text, which the product-name
rewrite does not reach.

Why: BACKLOG S-239, S-170.

Removable when: Chromium takes the product name from a placeholder there.
---
 chrome/app/generated_resources.grd | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/app/generated_resources.grd b/chrome/app/generated_resources.grd
index fa60a8e140fc7..d6c7921985ac9 100644
--- a/chrome/app/generated_resources.grd
+++ b/chrome/app/generated_resources.grd
@@ -18259,7 +18259,7 @@ Please help our engineers fix this problem. Tell us what happened right before y
       </message>
       <if expr="is_macosx">
         <message name="IDS_WEBAUTHN_YOUR_CHROME_PROFILE" desc="Menu item text. The user selects this to use a hardware-based authentication mechanism that is built in to the computer, such as a fingerprint reader. The credential itself is stored in the Chrome profile, however, and this text emphasizes that.">
-          Your Chrome profile
+          Your Stedding profile
         </message>
       </if>
       <message name="IDS_WEBAUTHN_TRANSPORT_INTERNAL" desc="Menu item text. The user selects this to use a hardware-based authentication mechanism that is built in to the computer, such as a fingerprint reader.">
@@ -18349,7 +18349,7 @@ Please help our engineers fix this problem. Tell us what happened right before y
 
       <if expr="is_macosx">
         <message name="IDS_WEBAUTHN_BLUETOOTH_PERMISSION" desc="Body text in a dialog that appears when the user has requested some function that depends on Bluetooth, but Chrome doesn't have permission to use Bluetooth. The action on this dialog is a button that will open the macOS System Settings so that the user can grant permission.">
-          Chrome needs permission to use Bluetooth to connect to your device
+          Stedding needs permission to use Bluetooth to connect to your device
         </message>
       </if>
 
@@ -18525,7 +18525,7 @@ Please help our engineers fix this problem. Tell us what happened right before y
         On other devices
       </message>
       <message name="IDS_WEBAUTHN_SOURCE_CHROME_PROFILE" desc="The subtitle shown in a button that lets the user select a passkey to sign in, indicating that the passkey resides in the user's Chrome Profile.">
-        Your Chrome profile
+        Your Stedding profile
       </message>
       <message name="IDS_WEBAUTHN_SOURCE_ICLOUD_KEYCHAIN" desc="The subtitle shown in a button that lets the user select a passkey to sign in, indicating that the passkey resides in Apple Passwords. Apple Passwords is an Apple brand and should be translated the same as it is in Apple devices. If you edit the language code in https://support.apple.com/es-es/104955 you can see how Apple translates it in several languages. ('Passwords' is usually localized.)">
         Apple Passwords
